(VAR-01: `a` or `an` before a type keyword declares a new variable. Both
 articles are accepted, and neither is checked against the word that
 follows: `an number` and `a apple` both compile. No builtin type keyword
 begins with a vowel, so `an` is only reachable at all on a user thing
 type or on a mismatched article.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox VAR-01.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   5
   7
   3
   3
)
A thing called apple has
  a number called weight is 3.

a number called plain is 5.
an number called mismatched is 7.
an apple called snack.
a apple called lunch.
Print plain.
Print mismatched.
Print snack's weight.
Print lunch's weight.
